                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f6f13125-ffb3-34ac-9291-39c20989dbad",
                        "entry_id": "20bf241b-7653-3688-b141-703fff5cadfc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Féminin singulier de vengeur."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "form-of"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e00a121f-ef89-4ba1-9a23-65ecc0a2fa7d",
                                "sense_id": "f6f13125-ffb3-34ac-9291-39c20989dbad",
                                "text": "Il mit quelque vengeresse intention dans la façon dont il prononça le mot « prédicateur », et Quatrebar, quand il s’avança, fut hué par les soldats, ce qui me donna à penser que le prieur, dans ses prêches à la Cathédrale, avait dû vouer plus d’une fois aux flammes de l’enfer et qui pis est, aux bûchers terrestres, nos frères huguenots."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "26b6c0ff-2506-4af8-ac1f-71eb269fcfa1",
                                "sense_id": "f6f13125-ffb3-34ac-9291-39c20989dbad",
                                "text": "Myriam se régale, de cette joie vengeresse que ressentent les enfants devant l’infortune des adultes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "32effbfa-baae-3754-b660-88e98ce4ffbb",
                "word": "vengeresse",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0da27bab-b7e3-4221-9f3d-0c13f0202001",
                        "entry_id": "32effbfa-baae-3754-b660-88e98ce4ffbb",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "vengeresses"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "9ee9137b-4fa0-4c4d-ba8e-31845132070e",
                        "entry_id": "32effbfa-baae-3754-b660-88e98ce4ffbb",
                        "tags": [
                            "masculine"
                        ],
                        "form": "vengeur"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "84043334-827a-3d16-a4ec-df1a014119f7",
                        "entry_id": "32effbfa-baae-3754-b660-88e98ce4ffbb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Celle qui venge, qui punit."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e2aee8bb-e3c2-43cd-946d-a302156b7821",
                                "sense_id": "84043334-827a-3d16-a4ec-df1a014119f7",
                                "text": "Je dois, moi, l’ancienne accusée, moi qui me suis tue, qui ai tout foulé aux pieds, ma vie, mon bonheur, mon amour, pour conserver un nom pur à l’enfant que j’avais vu naître, moi la condamnée, aujourd’hui la vengeresse de Marguerite et de mon frère, je dois vous apprendre tous les détails de la mort de M. de Sauvetat."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "979112b4-417e-4b31-b91a-dc0c629123c8",
                                "sense_id": "84043334-827a-3d16-a4ec-df1a014119f7",
                                "text": "Cependant, il n’en était pas encore à se repentir d’avoir pris parti pour la vengeresse d’Héva Nesbitt. Il restait même prêt à l’appuyer encore, quand viendrait le jour où elle réclamerait son aide."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0f85182d-ae31-4402-a11d-86628e9f2d9b",
                        "source_entry_id": "32effbfa-baae-3754-b660-88e98ce4ffbb",
                        "source_sense_id": "84043334-827a-3d16-a4ec-df1a014119f7",
                        "target_lang_word": "Rächerin",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Rächerin",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "22f8ab5a-a9d7-3908-bee9-4d4337a0af9a",
                                        "entry_id": "fd129b99-785c-3a9b-987b-4af8d6cb4e59",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "eine Frau, die Rache ausübt (die sich oder jemand anders rächt)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b492027-704d-4d58-b024-1727187827f9",
                                                "sense_id": "22f8ab5a-a9d7-3908-bee9-4d4337a0af9a",
                                                "text": "Nachdem man ihr das Liebste genommen hatte, wurde sie zur furchtlosen Rächerin."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6245092e-5026-4f5b-bcca-479f4a676d58",
                                                "sense_id": "22f8ab5a-a9d7-3908-bee9-4d4337a0af9a",
                                                "text": "„Dagegen mobilisiert Dahl nicht nur schauderhafte Bilder von Gewalt, sondern auch die ältesten Rachegöttinnen der europäischen Literatur. Wer seine Erynnien sind und warum diese zeitgenössischen Rächerinnen nicht, wie bei Aischylos die Eumeniden, von ihrer Rache ablassen können - das finden die modernen Kreuzritter der A-Gruppe nach und nach heraus.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "48afa049-9166-4055-893d-2d2df1b7440c",
                        "source_entry_id": "32effbfa-baae-3754-b660-88e98ce4ffbb",
                        "source_sense_id": "84043334-827a-3d16-a4ec-df1a014119f7",
                        "target_lang_word": "avengeress",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "avengeress",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d77272a6-6624-391f-9700-23edf9e43d3f",
                                        "entry_id": "e41bbfd8-7144-339f-92f1-ea45b5d0caf7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female avenger."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0af63fe-adc1-46d7-81f8-0a5e3dd69ebe",
                                                "sense_id": "d77272a6-6624-391f-9700-23edf9e43d3f",
                                                "text": "That cruell Queene avengeresse"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "495b0355-55e0-4cb6-bc41-beb061530d9a",
                                                "sense_id": "d77272a6-6624-391f-9700-23edf9e43d3f",
                                                "text": "Here you see the torch of Althaea, the avengeress; she was a good sister, but a bad mother."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "02d5d4ca-6024-4d92-8fc0-b534ef8488ee",
                        "source_entry_id": "32effbfa-baae-3754-b660-88e98ce4ffbb",
                        "source_sense_id": "84043334-827a-3d16-a4ec-df1a014119f7",
                        "target_lang_word": "vindicatress",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "vindicatress",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8f8ac7c8-3f16-39e2-be96-aa1914c92d82",
                                        "entry_id": "3e8885d4-0fc6-39e9-b0e1-0b58b88016eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female vindicator; a woman who vindicates."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f75fbafb-8681-4d99-b3ed-07ce2e7f0878",
                                                "sense_id": "8f8ac7c8-3f16-39e2-be96-aa1914c92d82",
                                                "text": "When our readers have gone through this article, and have heard us declare our perfect conviction of its truth; when they have heard us say, that it is agreeable, as far as it goes, with the enquiries which we have made, when they have further heard, that the scene of the brutal transaction was in a back room of the public-house above mentioned: that the parties had drawn the curtains to the room, but had left a part that the curtains did not cover but that might be seen through: that a little girl (vindicatress of her sex!) happening to go into the back court into which the window looked, Wondering to see the curtains drawn, had the curiosity to look in, where she saw the parties engaged in a way not to be described; that the little girl (better guardian of public morals than the \"respectable\" part of the press) ran to the landlord, who came out with other persons with him, who were all witnesses of the fact, to that certain extent, at least, of which the Observer speaks; that after this, the landlord and others laudably went, dashed in the door, took the parties in the state of Achilles as far as nakedness was necessary to their intentions; that they then dragged them to the watch-house, in that very same state: when our readers have heard all this, they will naturally cry aloud, 'why is the name of this Bishop suppressed?'"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed41ff80-2913-40da-9cb7-4843ab143c23",
                                                "sense_id": "8f8ac7c8-3f16-39e2-be96-aa1914c92d82",
                                                "text": "Had the vindicatress of the 'Rights of Women' lived in these days (fifty years later), when the iron pen is the almost universal instrument of writing, she would have bestowed upon Time a less common material for recording his doings."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
